1result.sql orders by the textual length of the duration field instead of its actual numeric value, so a time like `1:05` ( four characters ) could be preferred over `00:43` ( five characters ) even though it is longer.  
2result.sql is perfectly correct but contains an unnecessary CASE branch for `HH:MM:SS`, making it more verbose than required for the data set (all NXT title bouts are stored as `MM:SS`).  
0result.sql converts the `MM:SS` string into real seconds, sorts numerically, and is therefore both correct and the simplest of the reliable options.

```plaintext
0result.sql
```